# Git LFS tracking for COSMOS-AI.
#
# Principle: LFS carries dataset payloads and binary arrays only.  Source code, result
# tables, manifests and small JSON/CSV stay in ordinary Git, so that diffs remain
# reviewable and LFS storage is not spent on files that do not need it.
#
# GitHub limits that shape these patterns:
#   ordinary Git   warns above 50 MB, rejects above 100 MB per file
#   Git LFS        2 GB per file on Free/Pro/Team; 1 GB storage and 1 GB/month
#                  bandwidth on the free tier
# See README.md ("Datasets and Git LFS") for what is and is not in this repository.

# --- dataset payloads: the authoritative raw archives and their extractions ---
data/**/raw/**                  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/processed/**            filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- binary dataset and array formats anywhere under data/ ---
data/**/*.zip                   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/*.gz                    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/*.npy                   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/*.npz                   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/*.parquet               filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/*.h5                    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
data/**/*.pkl                   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- experiment arrays: write-once binaries, kept out of ordinary Git history ---
outputs/**/*.npy                filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
outputs/**/*.npz                filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
outputs/**/*.gz                 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# --- model weights and checkpoints, wherever they appear ---
*.pt                            filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pth                           filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ckpt                          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.onnx                          filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# NOTE: *.pptx is deliberately NOT in LFS.  The one slide deck here (5.5 MB) was already
# committed as an ordinary Git object before LFS was introduced; tracking the extension now
# would make `git lfs fsck` report the existing blob as a non-pointer, and converting it
# would mean rewriting history for no benefit at that size.

# Deliberately NOT in LFS: *.py, *.md, *.tex, *.bib, *.json, *.csv outside data/.
# Result tables are small and benefit from readable text diffs.

# --- line-ending and diff hygiene ---
# Source text is normalised to LF.  Data files are NOT: every dataset file is checksummed in
# data/DATASET_MANIFEST.csv, and end-of-line conversion would alter those bytes and break
# `python -m cosmos.ai.data.validate`.  Several CelesTrak CSVs genuinely use CRLF upstream.
*.py       text diff=python
*.md       text
*.tex      text
*.bib      text
*.csv      -text
*.tsv      -text
*.jsonl    -text
*.dat      -text
*.json     -text
*.pdf      binary
*.png      binary
*.docx     binary
*.pptx     binary
